{"input": "Summarize the discussion about the working design of the remote control.", "answers": ["The industrial designer described the product as a portable device with some energy source, an interface which included some pressing buttons and keys, a processor, some infrared source which could send the information to the main device, and different encryption codes for different TVs. Since the Marketing and the user interface designer mentioned speech recognition, the industrial designer also took that into account. All these components would cost 5 Euros or even less than that. As for gesture recognition and automatic power control, the group gave them up due to price issues. At the end of the meeting, the group also talked about how to enable the users to find the controller."], "length": 7341, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The discussion about the working design of the remote control focused on the technical aspects, including the energy source (battery), interface (buttons and infrared source), and chip (digital signal processing chip). The design aims to be simple, user-friendly, and cost-effective, with a focus on the T_V_ remote control. The team considered various features, such as automatic on/off control, speech recognition, and gesture recognition, but ultimately decided to prioritize the latter. They also discussed the potential for automatic on/off control and speech recognition, but noted that these features may be too expensive or complex for the current design."}
{"input": "What did the group talk about the touch screen under the limitation of the budget?", "answers": ["The group found that if they would use the touch screen as well as the voice recognition technique, the cost would up to 17 euros. On the other hand, in order to guarantee the one hundred percent profit, the price would be more than 30, which would risk losing potential consumers. Provided that they would control the cost within 12.5 euros, they would have to cut off some functions, for example, voice recognition. It was really hard to balance between the popular tastes, the cost and the quality."], "length": 7881, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The group decided to rule out the touch screen due to its high cost, with an estimated cost of €17.50 per remote control, which was above the budget of €12.50. They considered alternative options, such as voice recognition, which was seen as a more affordable and feasible solution within their budget constraints."}
{"input": "What was the general discussion?", "answers": ["The group discussed recognition results generated for 20 minutes of close-talking microphone data. Recognition performance was very good, indicating promising results for forced alignment procedures and the ability to analyze other important signal information, e.g. prosody and overlapping speech. It was decided that close-talking data should be downsampled and fed to the SRI recognizer to compare recognition performance, and that data from the far-field microphones should be tested on the recognizer as soon as possible. The group also discussed recording setup and equipment issues. "], "length": 12783, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The general discussion revolved around the progress of the speech recognition project, specifically the recognition of close-talking mikes and the use of a new microphone system. The team discussed the results of a recent meeting, where they tested the new microphone system and found that it worked well, but there were some issues with the recognition of certain words and phrases. They also talked about the need to adapt the language models to the specific dialects and accents of the speakers, and to improve the transcription process. Additionally, they discussed the possibility of using a wireless microphone system, which would allow speakers to move around freely during the meeting. The team also talked about the need to establish a global encoding standard for transcription, and to improve the accuracy of the recognition system."}
{"input": "Summarize the Project Manager's perspective on the prototype.", "answers": ["The Project Manager thought the prototype was basically the same with the former one, and the thickness was not suitable for the target customers. Then the LCD screen might be covered when held by hands, so the users couldn't figure out what happened on the screen. Therefore from this perspective the screen was totally unusable, still needing marketing research."], "length": 10667, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The Project Manager seems to be somewhat dissatisfied with the prototype, mentioning that it's \"not very interesting\" and that they had to redo some of the decisions. They also express frustration with the costs, particularly the high cost of the sample speaker, which they consider to be \"far, by far, the most expensive\" part of the project. However, they do acknowledge the design's potential and the team's efforts, and they seem to be willing to move forward with the project despite some reservations."}
