{"input": "What was concluded on semantic specification?", "answers": ["The revised semantic specification and construction formalism are more stable than the previous versions. In the latter, we find both construction types and meaning types along with formal considerations like verb subcategorization, or the ones a \"directed motion\" construction would dictate."], "length": 24580, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The participants concluded that the goal of the semantic specification is to fill out more and more of the bindings needed in order to come up with the final one, and that the actual constraint is related to the tourist domain and the kinds of interactions that might occur in the tourist domain, assuming that people are being helpful and not trying to deceive. They also decided to focus on getting it right in the short run, rather than trying to guess a inheritance structure and all that sort of stuff before they know what they're doing."}
{"input": "Summarize the meeting", "answers": ["The meeting concerned mostly status updates and logistical affairs. The participants learned that the transcription status was good. The progress on the DARPA demo was also good, except the interface did not look as pretty as they had wanted to. The storage disks, which they had been waiting for, had finally arrived, but the person responsible for installing them was going on break. The participants also decided to schedule less meetings, so they have updates to report when they do. The meeting ended with technical discussion about model performance."], "length": 12797, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting discussed the progress of the meeting recorder project, including the transcription status, the use of IBM's transcription service, and the need for more disk space to store the collected data. The team also discussed the use of the Transcriber interface, which was not working well due to compatibility issues with the Tcl-Tk library. The meeting also touched on the topic of recognition systems, including the use of the Hub-5 system and the tandem system, and the need to improve the performance of the recognition system. Additionally, the team discussed the use of the SRI system's alignments and the potential use of embedded training to improve the performance of the recognition system. The meeting concluded with a discussion of the need for more disk space and the potential use of a smaller net with fewer parameters to improve the performance of the recognition system."}
