ng the Meeting Recorder system to study the behavior of speakers in meetings, including the use of the system to analyze the audio and identify overlapping speech.\n9. The consideration of using the Meeting Recorder system to study the behavior of speakers in meetings, including the use of the system to analyze the audio and identify overlapping speech.\n10. The discussion of the potential for using the Meeting Recorder system to study the behavior of speakers in meetings, including the use of the system to analyze the audio and identify overlapping speech."}
{"input": "Summarize the discussion about hourly rates of the service.", "answers": ["In this part, the meeting talked about the affordability of £4.50 amount (the universal amount) and add-ups for some cases. The group separately discussed the situation of families of different incomes levels and different areas."], "length": 12329, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The discussion about hourly rates of the childcare service focused on the £4.50 rate per hour, which was set as a universal rate for all providers. The Minister, Huw Irranca-Davies, acknowledged that this rate may not be sufficient for more expensive areas, such as Cardiff and Newport, where costs are higher, and that there may be a need for a higher rate in those areas. However, he also stated that the £4.50 rate has been welcomed by the sector and that it is suitable for the foreseeable future. The Minister also mentioned that the rate does not cover additional costs such as food, transport, and consumables, and that there are plans to review the rate in the future if necessary."}
{"input": "What was Kirsty Williams' opinion of the decision of not accrediting the University of South Wales with the ability to deliver teacher training?", "answers": ["Kirsty Williams thought this process was independent of the Government, and it would not be very appropriate to comment on it. From the very outset of their ITE reforms, they had made it clear that they expected very high standards in the ITE system, but this process was independent of the Government. More specifically with the concern of the impact on students and staff, Kirsty Williams mentioned that this would be a responsibility of University of South Wales itself."], "length": 13885, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "Kirsty Williams stated that she is not in a position to comment on the decision, as it is an independent process, and that she has confidence in the people appointed by the Education Workforce Council (EWC) to undertake the process. She also acknowledged that the decision may have an impact on students and staff, but emphasized that the Welsh Government will commission training places from accredited institutions."}
{"input": "What did Vaughan Gething think of the mental health recovery plan when talking about the ways of continuing mental health service during the lockdown?", "answers": ["When it comes to continuing mental health service during the lockdown, Vaughan Gething insisted that it was of great necessity to carry out a mental health recovery plan that with such a system, government can ensure the children could enjoy a healthy mental state during the school lockdown. However, at present they had not yet finished a detailed research in this job for that they were still under the cooperation with health boards to get a whole perspective of the situation."], "length": 10510, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "Vaughan Gething stated that the mental health recovery plan would be of \"very real importance\" to him, as he was concerned about the potential long-term damage to children and young people's mental health and well-being due to the pandemic, and he emphasized the need for a flexible and ongoing approach to supporting mental health services during the lockdown."}
{"input": "What did Huw Irranca-Davies think about the capacity in the next several years to deliver the product when talking about childcare offer?", "answers": ["Huw Irranca-Davies thought there would be capacity growth in the next two to three years to deliver the product. The confidence was constructed by the development of roll-out, in which the team was learning live time. Moreover, there was a separate fund into cycle meithrin to address the issue of the Welsh language."], "length": 12342, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "Huw Irranca-Davies AM expressed confidence that the workforce capacity to meet the childcare offer's requirements could be delivered within the next two to three years, citing the 10-year workforce development plan and the £60 million capital fund allocated to childcare facilities. He also mentioned that the Welsh Government had engaged with local authorities and childcare providers to identify areas of need and develop strategies to address them, and that the sector understood the economic impact of the scheme and the benefits it would bring."}
{"input": "What did the User Interface think about their previous suggestions when discussing the user interface?", "answers": ["The User Interface affirmed their previous efforts at first, but he thought that was not enough, so he went on to propose that they might consider buying another face plate and include a touch screen. In terms of the buttons on the screen, the User Interface found the existing problem that some of the buttons would be stuck in the screen and not so easy to be found and touched, so he suggested making those essential buttons in conspicuous colours like red."], "length": 7881, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The User Interface seemed to be open to their previous suggestions, as they stated \"I think to a certain extent we have to stick with uh kind of uh a little bit traditional in terms of the buttons and then and then make our unique feature our casing and what not and our voice command\" and also mentioned that they were \"willing to agree with everything that's been said\". They also seemed to be on board with the idea of having a non-remote-looking remote control, saying \"Well what are we actually doing?... Yeah, totally\"."}
{"input": "Why did the group think of the locator when presenting the functional requirements?", "answers": ["When Marketing mentioned about the long battery life, the group came up with the locator that the remote could beep when users clapped. Also, this function should be designed to not beep every five minutes so that users would not like the remote. The group mates agreed on it and thought it was an interesting and excellent idea."], "length": 8489, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The group thought of the locator as a feature that could be included in the remote control to help locate it when it's lost or misplaced, as it would allow the user to press a button and hear a beep, making it easier to find the remote control."}
{"input": "Summarize what was said about the microphone data", "answers": ["The group discussed recognition results generated for 20 minutes of close-talking microphone data. Recognition performance was very good, indicating promising results for forced alignment procedures and the ability to analyze other important signal information, e.g. prosody and overlapping speech. It was decided that close-talking data should be downsampled and fed to the SRI recognizer to compare recognition performance, and that data from the far-field microphones should be tested on the recognizer as soon as possible."], "length": 12786, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The discussion about microphone data centered around the use of close-talking microphones for the project. It was mentioned that the current setup uses a single microphone for each speaker, which can lead to issues with overlapping talk and echo cancellation. The group considered using wireless microphones, but ultimately decided to stick with the current setup. They also discussed the possibility of using a different type of microphone, such as a headset with a built-in microphone, but this was not pursued further. Additionally, it was noted that the current microphones are not very comfortable to wear, and that a hand-held microphone might be a better option. The group also considered the issue of recording the meeting and transcribing it, with some suggesting that it would be easier to do this with a digital recorder."}
{"input": "What did the user interface designer propose in the discussion about industrial components?", "answers": ["Although the industrial designer regarded LCD as costly, the user interface designer proposed adding an LCD as a kind of output that only displayed some information or menu and was not touch sensitive, which might reduce the cost."], "length": 6961, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The user interface designer proposed using a combination of materials, such as titanium and rubber, to create a unique and functional design for the remote control. Specifically, they suggested using titanium panels on a rubber body, or vice versa, to achieve the desired look and feel. They also explored the idea of using a spongy or curved shape, similar to a fruit, to add a new dimension to the design."}
{"input": "What did Huw Irranca-Davies think about the affordability of lowest-income working families when talking about hourly rates of the service?", "answers": ["Huw Irranca-Davies thought £4.50amount was an appropriate and universal amount. As for the add-ons, even low-income families could discriminate between providers. Also, the team would be substantially transparent thus parents can make the decisions."], "length": 12340, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "Huw Irranca-Davies stated that the £4.50 hourly rate was suitable for the foreseeable future, and that the feedback from organizations such as the Professional Association for Childcare and Early Years and the National Day Nurseries Association Wales suggested that this rate was appropriate. However, he also acknowledged that the national living wage was increasing and that the rate might not be enough in the future, and that there was a risk that the scheme could price out the most disadvantaged families if add-ons were charged."}
{"input": "What did the group discuss about the design goal of the remote control?", "answers": ["They wanted it to be original, trendy, user-friendly, durable, creative and characteristic, so it can be very intuitive that people could use the product. In addition, the price, cost and expected profit of the remote control were also determined. In the part of creativity, they pointed out that creativity should have its own characteristics and ensure its fashion without affecting its functionality, so as to truly \"introduce fashion into electronics\". In terms of function, it is necessary to simplify the switch and guarantee function."], "length": 3976, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The group discussed that the remote control should be original, trendy, and user-friendly, with a focus on providing a unique and intuitive design. They also considered the idea of simplifying the remote control by reducing the number of buttons and incorporating a menu-based system, which would make it easier for users to navigate and use. Additionally, they touched upon the idea of aiming for a high battery life, but ultimately decided not to stray too far from the usual design of remote controls to ensure a smooth user experience."}
{"input": "How would the allocation contribute to educational research?", "answers": ["To start with, Bethan Owen first pointed out that figures showed that the percentage of income that had come from research in Wales was smaller than that in England, so the Welsh universities were receiving less of the money that was available, which was a factor that resulted from having less QR as a percentage. To tackle this issue, the government had provided funding in 2017-18 and 2018-19 to WISERD Education, which was a research collaboration between a number of the Welsh universities, specifically looking at educational issues. However, it was still early to see how allocation for 2019-20 would work."], "length": 10200, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The allocation for 2019-20 will provide £15 million back into the sector in innovation funding, which is intended to improve universities' ability to access funding from UKRI (Innovate UK), and also support educational research."}
{"input": "What's the decision of remote feature design?", "answers": ["Project Manager believed that it could not be heavy. Industrial Designer indicated that fewer and bigger buttons are better and should be bust-free, for instance, rubber could be used on it. Industrial Designer also suggested that when users push a button, they could hear some sort of bleep. User Interface suggested a LED on the corner and not too expensive material like plastic could be used. Marketing added that it should look nice for better sales and should work with as many as possible of existing products listed on their website. Industrial Designer also concluded that it should be battery-saving."], "length": 1789, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The design of the remote control will have a few key features, including a simple and user-friendly interface with big buttons, a LED light on the corner to indicate when the remote is working, and a design that is not too heavy or bulky. The remote control should also be compatible with other devices, such as TVs and video recorders, and should be easy to use and maintain. Additionally, the design should be aesthetically pleasing and should not require frequent battery changes."}
{"input": "Summarize the whole meeting.", "answers": ["This meeting is about some final decisions on the design of the remote control. It started with presentations on the conceptual design from Marketing, Industrial Designer, and User Interface, and had a discussion on the decisions about the control. The Project Manager put a file in his folder to place the kind of decisions they should take."], "length": 11169, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting was a discussion about designing a remote control for a new electronic device. The team went over various aspects such as the material for the back and front, the design of the buttons, the LCD screen, and the overall look and feel of the device. They also discussed the importance of making the device trendy and fashionable, with a focus on bright colors and a futuristic design. The team decided on a titanium back and a plastic front, with a touch-sensitive screen and a simple interface. They also discussed the use of a logo and slogan on the device, with the slogan \"We put the fashion in electronics\" being chosen. The meeting concluded with the team agreeing on the design and the project manager assigning tasks to the team members, including the industrial designer and the user interface designer."}
{"input": "Summarize the decision of the discussion about the design goal of the remote control.", "answers": ["The group hoped that it can be applied to children, in particular to ensure their safety during use. Besides, it should be colourful and beautiful to attract the attention of children. The price also should be reasonable and affordable, not too expensive, but the profit can be guaranteed. In terms of function design, unnecessary functions and switches should be removed to enhance their applicability."], "length": 3239, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The discussion about the design goal of the remote control focused on several key aspects, including functionality, usability, and aesthetics. The team decided that the remote control should be user-friendly, with a simple and intuitive interface, and should be able to adapt to the user's preferences. They also discussed the importance of robustness and durability, with a focus on making it resistant to accidental presses and damage. Additionally, they considered the need for a \"brain\" or software component to enable advanced features such as recording and playback of sequences of actions. The team also agreed that the remote control should be colorful and have a unique design, with a focus on making it visually appealing and easy to use. Overall, the goal is to create a remote control that is both functional and user-friendly, with a focus on making it accessible to a wide range of users."}
{"input": "How did Eluned Morgan respond to whether wishing to see people have greater pay equality between schoolteachers and FE when discussing the pay dispute situation?", "answers": ["Eluned Morgan said that they would wish to see pay equality in relation to teaching. As for whether all staff should get the increase or only teaching staff but not non-teaching staff, Eluned Morgan thought this should be up to ColegauCymru to negotiate and to discuss, and they should wait for their outcomes."], "length": 13887, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "Eluned Morgan stated that she believed in pay equality in relation to teaching, but did not explicitly state that she wished for all staff, including non-teaching staff, to have equal pay. She said that the issue of pay equality was up to ColegauCymru to negotiate and discuss with the trade unions, and that she would wait to see what the outcomes were before responding formally."}
{"input": "Summarize the review of some problems from the past meetings.", "answers": ["The group briefly talked about their agreements of the past meetings. They were all concerned with the interchangeable user interfaces and they agreed to make it more natural-looking and multi-faces. The Industrial Design then mentioned the issue of the material. They decided to use a rubber coat in case the remote control would be damaged when being dropped occasionally. After most details were checked, the Project Manager turned to the budget problem. It is quite essential for them to be both environmentally friendly and economic."], "length": 9188, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The team discussed some issues from previous meetings, including the lack of clear minutes from the previous meeting, which led to confusion and uncertainty. They also noted that the project was not well-structured, with too much information coming in at the last minute, making it difficult to keep up. Additionally, the team felt that they didn't have enough time to brainstorm and discuss ideas thoroughly, leading to some ideas being overlooked or not fully explored."}
{"input": "What did the group think of disposable income when discussing general requirements?", "answers": ["Industrial Designer suggested they should also look up popularity among the 25 to 35 years old age group if they looked into a stylish design. Marketing said it was 70% popular among this age group and thought this age group didn't have much economic burden so the remote price should not be unaffordable. User Interface supplemented that their remote might not function with the old TV. Therefore, the group decided to include both 15 to 25 and 25 to 35 years old age group into consideration."], "length": 8488, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The group discussed the relationship between disposable income and the target audience for the remote control. They noted that younger people, particularly those between 15 to 35 years old, have a higher disposable income and are more likely to pay more for a voice recognition remote control. This suggests that the group considers disposable income to be an important factor in determining the target audience for the product."}
{"input": "What is the conclusion of the discussion about Marketing strategy when discussing group's plan of their marketing strategy?", "answers": ["The team decided that the remote had to be compatible with most of the world's TVS, or at least the ones they made. And the buttons must be internationally recognized.They also thought that the function of the remote control was to change the state of the TV and this could be realized by pressing the button."], "length": 6395, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The conclusion of the discussion about marketing strategy is that the group wants to make their remote control original, trendy, and modern, and to be compatible with different systems, including D_V_D_ players and T_V_ sets, and they also want to make it universal and easy to use, with a simple and recognizable design, such as a standard front, and they plan to use different colors to make it appealing to different audiences, including young people and families with children."}
{"input": "Why did the marketing think they should aim at young people?", "answers": ["Because in general the early adopters of a new device were young people and teletext was used less among the young than the elderly. Plus, the young found it very relevant to have speech recognition in their remote control so that they could just tell the controller what they wanted instead of zapping."], "length": 7341, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The marketing expert, Sammy Benjo, thought that they should aim at young people because they are more likely to be interested in a new device, and as a general rule, early adopters of new technology tend to be young people."}
{"input": "Summarize the discussion about the early implementer areas.", "answers": ["Huw Irranca-Davies said the process of early implementer areas had gone well and were encouraged to expand. Two things had been learned during this process by their team. To respond to the questioner, Huw Irranca-Davies then further explained the administrative burden they met and expressed a confident attitude in addressing that. The next question answered was about the spread issue of this project."], "length": 12328, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The discussion about the early implementer areas focused on the challenges faced by these areas in implementing the childcare offer. The Minister, Huw Irranca-Davies, acknowledged that the early implementer areas were experiencing difficulties in administering the scheme, particularly in terms of the administrative burden and communication with parents and providers. He also mentioned that the intensity of demand for services was not spread evenly across the areas, with some experiencing higher demand than others. The Minister emphasized that the Welsh Government was learning from these early experiences and was working to address the challenges and improve the roll-out of the scheme."}
{"input": "What did Julie Morgan elaborate on the online survey when talking about the evaluations on the legitimacy of the children's rights, protection and demands?", "answers": ["When discussing the evaluations on the legitimacy of the children's rights, protection and demands, Julie Morgan mentioned that they had carried out an online survey to look into the children's thoughts and demands over the pandemic.The survey involved what did the children do through the lockdown, what they thought about the measures that Welsh government and their schools had taken, and whether they were looking for the reschooling. With those questions, the group was meant to have a more overall idea of the children's rights and demands in order to care for them better during this period."], "length": 10510, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "Julie Morgan elaborated that the online survey, which is being conducted in conjunction with the children's commissioner and Young Wales, aims to gather the views of children on the COVID-19 situation, their experiences, and their perceptions of the measures taken to protect their rights and well-being."}
{"input": "Summarize discussion about the desired features of remote control.", "answers": ["The team came up with some general desired features about their new TV remote controls,including compatibility, appearance and functions .First, they thought compatibility is of importance.Second ,they thought good looks and sizes of remote controls were two vital features .Third, buttons should be designed properly."], "length": 6386, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The desired features of the remote control include being original, trendy, and modern, with a focus on being user-friendly and easy to learn, especially for people from different cultures. The remote control should have a universal design that can work with various brands and systems, including D_V_D_ players and T_V_ sets. It should also have a simple and recognizable design, with a standard front that can be easily customized with different colors or designs. The remote control should have a comfortable and ergonomic design, with buttons that are not too small or too large, and have a precise and responsive feel. Additionally, it should have a universal way of transmitting signals to the television, such as infrared beams, and should be compatible with different types of televisions and D_V_D_ players."}
{"input": "Which color was considered more appropriate by team members when discussing the desired features of remote control?", "answers": ["They argue that the TV remote should not be too colorful and must match the color of the TV they sell. They admit that no color is acceptable to everyone. It's something they think people generally don't like bright colors. It's their intention to make the TV remote in black or gray or silver."], "length": 6394, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The color grey or black was considered more appropriate by team members when discussing the desired features of the remote control. They mentioned that people generally accept and prefer these colors, and that using bright colors like pink might not be well-received."}
{"input": "Why did the Industrial Designer disagree to replace the titanium when discussing product cost and quotation?", "answers": ["The Industrial Designer suggested that the titanium provided the tough look and the strong cover to protect the product. Besides, the older customers would like it much more because it fit their taste. So the titanium was important and shouldn't be replacing by titanium-like plastic or saving the LCD screen but dumping the titanium."], "length": 10675, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The Industrial Designer disagreed to replace the titanium with plastic because he believed that the titanium provided a tough look and feel, which was important for older people, and that it was a key feature of the product's design. He also thought that the titanium was useful for the product's durability and strength."}
{"input": "Summarize the ways of continuing mental health service during the lockdown.", "answers": ["Vaughan Gething pointed out that due to the school lockdown, children as well as their parents would face difficulties at home learning and social-contacting. In case they would suffer from potential mental health problems, the government have to carry out a mental health recovery plan. Sian Gwenllian then mentioned that the CAMHS, as well as all the schools, should follow up the mental states of children and offer telephone and online support."], "length": 10497, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The Welsh Government has continued to provide mental health services during the lockdown, including online support services and telephone support services, which have been expanded to reach more people. The health visitor service has also not stopped, and has consolidated its Healthy Child Wales Programme to maintain contact with families, particularly those with vulnerable children. Additionally, the perinatal mental health service has continued to provide support to new mothers and their families, with services being delivered online or via telephone where possible. The Government has also ensured that children and young people have access to technology to maintain contact with social workers and other support workers and networks."}
{"input": "Summarize the discussion about the design of remote control for children.", "answers": ["The group thought remote controls should keep children safe while using them. At the same time, the remote control should be brightly coloured. Even if it is not colourful, it should also choose a monochrome colour that children like to attract them."], "length": 3236, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The discussion about the design of a remote control for children focused on making it user-friendly, robust, and safe for kids. The team considered features such as a small size, colorful design, and easy-to-use interface, with the goal of preventing accidental button presses and making it easy for children to navigate. They also discussed the importance of a \"go back\" button and a \"history\" feature to allow children to undo previous actions, and considered the possibility of a universal remote control that could be adapted to different user needs. Additionally, the team touched on the idea of a \"brain\" or software-based remote control that could learn the child's preferences and adapt to their needs over time."}
{"input": "What was the solution to risk appetite?", "answers": ["Dr David Blaney believed that governing bodies were not likely to exhibit as an imprudent risk appetite since they would see the potential risks coming through in forecasts, in requests for borrowings, predominantly and many other ways. Although the government body included a slightly different perspective, divisions were not falling short. Besides, commitments from enthusiastic people and occasionally with a slightly external perspective would also be a help."], "length": 10199, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The solution to risk appetite is not a straightforward one, but rather a nuanced approach that involves the governing bodies of universities being encouraged to engage in a process of \"constructive challenge\" and to ask the right questions. This is achieved through the provision of a toolkit by HEFCW that locates institutions in the context of the UK, and through the encouragement of independent review of governance in Wales. Additionally, HEFCW has a role as an \"honest broker\" to provide external perspectives and to help governing bodies make informed decisions. The sector is also expected to take ownership of this process and to engage in a culture of openness and transparency."}
{"input": "What did the industrial designer recommend when discussing industrial components and why?", "answers": ["The industrial designer recommended batteries instead of solar cells because it would be problematic if solar cells didn't have enough energy. Titanium was proposed rather than rubber as the latter would make it difficult to do the moulding of buttons. Besides, the industrial designer wanted a simple push button because it only needed a simple chip and was less expensive than LCD."], "length": 6960, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The industrial designer recommended using a simple battery instead of solar cells, titanium instead of rubber, and push buttons instead of L_C_D_ displays. This was because the designer believed that these options would be more cost-effective and easier to manufacture, allowing for a more affordable and user-friendly remote control."}
{"input": "Why did the Project Manager agree with Marketing when discussing his personal ideas towards the design?", "answers": ["The Marketing proposed to use voice control on the remote and according to his research, three quarters of people under 35 are in favour of voice control. At the same time, in order to keep the remote not so easy to be lost as its counterparts of other brands, voice control would be an essential technique. For those two reasons, the Marketing persuaded the Project Manager to target their consumers as the youth."], "length": 5340, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The Project Manager agreed with Marketing when discussing his personal ideas towards the design because he acknowledged that the idea of using a touch screen with a simple and easy-to-use interface, such as the company logo, would be a good way to make the remote control user-friendly and aesthetically pleasing, and would also help to improve the battery life."}
{"input": "What was the final decision of the discussion about automatic power control?", "answers": ["The industrial designer thought the automatic power control would be a bit problematic because there were different criteria for different people. Then the marketing proposed that they should design a personalized product so that the users could have their own settings. The proposal was accepted by the industrial designer but later the idea of automatic power control was still abandoned because of price issues."], "length": 7342, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The final decision was that automatic power control was not possible due to the power consumption and potential interference with other devices, and it was decided to focus on other features such as speech recognition and gesture recognition."}
{"input": "Summarize the group discussion about general requirements.", "answers": ["The group had a discussion about the target age group and they agreed to look at 15 to 35 year olds. Also, they decided to make it look simple, but still have those key buttons so it would be easy to use. Lastly, the group agreed to include one sort of menu button and voice recognition as an option."], "length": 8483, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The group discussion focused on the general requirements of the remote control, including its design, functionality, and user interface. The main goals were to create a simple, easy-to-use remote control that would be compatible with most televisions and would not be too expensive. The group considered various options, including voice recognition, but ultimately decided to keep the remote control simple with major buttons and a menu option, with voice recognition as an optional feature. They also discussed the importance of making the remote control look stylish and fashionable, particularly for the 15-35 age group. The group decided to target this age group and make the remote control easy to use, but not too complicated."}
{"input": "Summarize the whole meeting.", "answers": ["This was a Children, Young People and Education Committee, and it was the scrutiny session with a focus on higher and further education. This whole meeting was conducted in a question and answer format. They firstly started with a question related to the trend of secondary school teachers recruiting situations, and the reasons for this, and the steps they had taken to mitigate this trend. Then they had a discussion on the decision made by the education workforce council not to accredit the University of South Wales with the ability to deliver teacher training. After this, there were some questions and answers related to the reform and reconfiguration of the post-16 education sector, equality of opportunity and university mergers. In addition, the parity of esteem between academic and vocational post-16 education and funding allocation were also discussed. Then they talked about the regional skills partnerships and the pay dispute situation. At last, they shared some opinions on 'legalised cheating'."], "length": 13866, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting was a scrutiny session with a focus on higher and further education in Wales, where the Cabinet Secretary for Education, Kirsty Williams, and the Minister for Children, Older People and Social Care, Eluned Morgan, answered questions from Members of the Senedd. The discussion covered various topics, including teacher training and recruitment, the impact of the £12.5 million cut in funding for further education colleges, the parity of esteem between academic and vocational post-16 education, and the pay dispute in the further education sector. The committee also discussed the need for more investment in degree and Master's-level apprenticeships, the importance of supporting students' mental health and well-being, and the issue of essay mills and academic misconduct. The meeting concluded with the committee resolving to meet in private for the remainder of the meeting to discuss further education and training reforms, including the Childcare Funding (Wales) Bill and the task and finish group on a whole-school approach to mental health."}
{"input": "Summarize the presentation and discussion about the technical design.", "answers": ["Industrial designer introduced the working design including the energy, LED sender, different user interface, and the chipboard with buttons on it. They could put every button under the thumb with an RSI. Then, the group discussed and decided to have removable fronts, a small centralized LCD screen, and a power button with 10 other setting buttons."], "length": 11304, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The presentation and discussion about the technical design of the remote control focused on the user interface and functionality. The team discussed the importance of a user-friendly design, with a focus on making the most commonly used buttons easily accessible. They also considered the need for a small LCD screen to display information, such as channel numbers and settings, and the importance of a menu button to access additional features. The team decided to place the LCD screen at the top of the remote control, with the most important buttons, such as power, channel, and volume, located at the bottom. They also discussed the need for a \"Save\" button and a menu system to access additional features, such as contrast and brightness settings. The team also considered the use of a \"Okay\" button for menu navigation and the placement of other buttons, such as the \"Chief\" button, in the menu system."}
{"input": "What did the Minister of Seniors say about pandemic assistance for seniors?", "answers": ["The Minister of Seniors clarified that his office recognizes that seniors are in great need. The minister explained that those receiving OAS and GIS are getting payments of $200 and $300 respectively. The minister was insistent that this was not an insignificant amount."], "length": 23789, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The Minister of Seniors, Deb Schulte, stated that the government is taking significant action to provide Canadian seniors with greater financial security and help them during the pandemic. She mentioned that the government is introducing a one-time tax-free payment of $300 for those who receive Old Age Security (OAS) and $200 for those receiving the Guaranteed Income Supplement (GIS), totaling $500 to seniors who receive both. Additionally, she mentioned that the government is investing in other charities and community-based projects to improve the quality of life for seniors."}
