{"input": "What did the user interface designer recommend to do when discussing technical function design?", "answers": ["The user interface designer recommended to have a screen with a backlight which could change colours and to put all the options into this screen so that few buttons were needed and users would find it easy to use. As for the material, titanium was preferred because it was unbreakable and baby-proof. The user interface designer also suggested making the power and volume control fully automatic."], "length": 7344, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The user interface designer recommended to use Occam's Razor, which means to make the remote control as simple as possible, with only the necessary functions, and to avoid over-complicating it."}
{"input": "Summarize the whole meeting.", "answers": ["The meeting was about a preliminary idea of new remote control, covering the price, the functions, the appearance and the name. After a brief self-introduction, Project Manager assigned the task. One of the most important issues of the meeting was about the price. Project Manager supposed the product should be sold at 25 euros with a one hundred percent profit. As it would be a multifunctional remote control, the members were confident that it would stand alone. Moving on to the issue of the appearance, the group analyzed the problems of the existing remotes and briefly talked about the user interface as well as came up with a name of the product."], "length": 5977, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting was a brainstorming session for a new project to design a universal remote control that can control various devices such as TVs, DVD players, and other electronics. The team discussed the project's goals, trade-offs, and initial ideas, including the use of a touch-screen interface, multi-format capabilities, and a sleek design. They also considered factors such as material quality, pricing, and target audience, with the aim of creating a product that is both functional and user-friendly. The team decided to focus on a 25-euro price point and explored ideas for a locator device and a design that would appeal to a wide range of users, including \"grandmas\" who may be less familiar with new technology. The meeting concluded with a plan to continue working on the project and to consult the project documents for a reminder of the initial ideas and trade-offs discussed."}
