{"input": "Summarize the whole meeting", "answers": ["The meeting was about a computer based navigation system that will be used to conduct linguistic experiments on navigational terminology and intentionality, and it was simultaneously being recorded for another project. The navigational interface allows people to walk around a place and perform basic actions, like entering a building. Its goal is to understand what people intend to do based on granular linguistic features. The experimental set up is that people talk to a human assistant who controls the program in an attempt to complete a certain task. To study intentionality, the team will determine important linguistic features and use a Bayes model to see if they can predict the intention based on utterances."], "length": 15403, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting discussed the project Meeting Recorder, which aims to create a system that can record and analyze meetings. The system will use a belief net to infer the intentions of participants, such as going to see a place, entering a building, or coming close to it. The meeting also discussed the data collection process, which involves recording subjects interacting with a computer system that provides them with tasks to complete. The system will be tested with a sample data set, and the results will be used to refine the belief net. The meeting also touched on the topic of changing the table to make the system work in English, and the potential for the system to be used in real-world applications, such as navigation systems. The meeting concluded with a plan to have the two participants work on the project, using the sample data set and refining the belief net based on their findings."}
