{"input": "Summarize the whole meeting.", "answers": ["The group mainly talked about the extra deciding of the product at this meeting including the presentation of the prototype assessment, the discussion of the requirements and trends of marketing and the product cost and quotation. Firstly, the Industrial Designer introduced the prototype of the product. It had not only the round basic shape which was made of hard plastics and titanium using different colors, but also the buttons like channel and volumn. Later, the group discussed some details and changes of redesigning the logo, buttons and screens. Next, the Marketing Expert mentioned the exterior of the product, the material attraction, and how easy it was to learn or use the basic functions of the product. Besides, the group discussed some details of the cost of components and made the product cheaper by replacing the titanium by hard plastics with similar color. They finally got an estimate of fourteen point one Euros, which was above the budget. In the end, they discussed the distinction between the product and other devices, and celebrated the completion of the project."], "length": 10663, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting was a discussion about a project, specifically a remote control device, with a focus on its design, functionality, and costs. The team went over the device's features, including its user interface, design, and functionality, and discussed the costs of producing it. They also talked about the challenges of implementing certain features, such as the L_C_D_ screen and the digital pen, and how they would impact the device's cost and functionality. The team also discussed the importance of the device's design and how it would appeal to the target audience. The meeting concluded with the team deciding to proceed with the project, but with some reservations about the costs and feasibility of certain features."}
{"input": "Summarize the discussion about industrial components.", "answers": ["The industrial designer provided several options respectively for energy, material and interface. Among these options, the industrial designer preferred traditional battery, titanium and simple push buttons so that they would have enough money for speech recognition. After that, the user interface designer proposed an LCD display only for output, which might be taken into account. The group also talked about how to enable the users to find their controllers."], "length": 6954, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The discussion about industrial components focused on the choice between titanium and rubber for the remote control's casing. The team considered the trend of using fruit and vegetable-inspired designs, with some members suggesting a spongy, fruit-like shape. However, they also noted that titanium is a more expensive material and may be difficult to work with due to its double-curved shape limitations. Ultimately, the team decided to explore both options, with one member suggesting using titanium panels on a rubber body, and another proposing a spongy, fruit-like shape."}
{"input": "What did the Industrial Designer recommend to do when discussing the naming of remote control and why?", "answers": ["After coming up with the idea of multi plates, the Industrial Designer asked to give the remote control a name and patent it. Within a brief discussion, they named it as Leopard Print out of the hope that it would also be helpful in cold winter days."], "length": 5990, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The Industrial Designer recommended to come up with a \"fuzzy\" name for the face plate, suggesting something like \"leopard print\" as an example, and also suggested patenting a name for it."}
{"input": "What did the team think about the new idea of Industrial Designer concerning the cover of the device?", "answers": ["Industrial Designer suggested having a trendy remote control with bright color, red for instance. But Marketing argued that it might add to cost and make it more difficult to design if the cover were to be changed. Industrial Designer also suggested that young people could draw on the cover to make their own remote control more unique. But again, it was questioned by User Interface who were not sure about whether it would be profitable."], "length": 4765, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The team was divided on the idea of having a cover for the device, with some members, like the User Interface and Marketing, thinking it could be a good idea to make it trendy and customizable, while others, like the Industrial Designer, were skeptical about the cost and practicality of it. The Industrial Designer mentioned that it would be difficult to design and would add to the cost, and the Project Manager ultimately decided that it was not a priority."}
