{"input": "Summarize the presentations on working design, technical functions, functional requirements.", "answers": ["Firstly, Industrial Designer presented on working design, identifying a few basic components of the remote. From the functional design perspective, Industrial Designer introduced what exactly the components were and how they worked with each other. Next, User Interface presented on technical functions design and personally suggested a small size of remote, red in colour and easy to use with must-have buttons. Then, Marketing presented on functional requirements and suggested the group aiming at both the functionality and beauty of the remote."], "length": 8486, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The Industrial Designer presented a working design of the remote control, identifying basic components and their functions, and explained how they work together. The User Interface presented a technical functions design, discussing the importance of buttons, channel selection, volume, and power, and how they can be implemented in a user-friendly manner. The User Interface also presented a functional requirements design, discussing the need for a simple and easy-to-use remote control with major buttons and a menu option, and the potential inclusion of voice recognition as an option."}
{"input": "Summarize their evaluations on the legitimacy of the children's rights, protection and demands.", "answers": ["In terms of their evaluations on the legitimacy of the children's rights, protection and demands, it was said that the group was launching a survey of children to see what the children were thinking over the outbreak of the COVID-19. The survey was carried online, asking mainly about whether the students were willing to go back to school and how they view other related problems. However, there were still indeed some drawbacks of their evaluations over the coronavirus Act. For example, the group thought that they should go further and view the laws from a future perspective, and assess each case individually more closely."], "length": 10499, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The Ministers and officials evaluated the legitimacy of children's rights, protection, and demands as a high priority, with Vaughan Gething AM stating that the mental health recovery plan will be of \"very real importance\" to him, and Julie Morgan AM assuring that the Welsh Government is committed to protecting children's rights, including those of vulnerable children and young people. They also acknowledged the challenges posed by the pandemic, including the impact on childcare services, and expressed concern about the potential for long-term damage to children's mental health and well-being. The Ministers also highlighted the importance of ensuring that all children have access to necessary technology to maintain contact with social workers and other key workers, and that support services are available to meet the needs of children and young people."}
{"input": "Summarize the discussion on storage disks and computer connections", "answers": ["The participants learned that the storage disks had eventually arrived. They were waiting on the disks to be installed. Grad E volunteered storage space on their own computer for the meantime. The meetings were around 1.5 gigs uncompressed and .5 gigs compressed. So, the group needed substantial space. The professor encouraged the team members to talk to Dave, the person responsible for managing the organization's storage systems, and figure things out."], "length": 12803, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The discussion on storage disks and computer connections centered around the need for more storage space for the meeting data. It was mentioned that the current system was running out of space, particularly on the Abbott disk server, and that additional storage was needed. The group considered using external hard drives, such as SUN-Blades, to increase storage capacity. However, it was noted that setting up these external drives would require additional time and effort. The group also discussed the possibility of using the ICSI net, but it was determined that this would not be feasible due to a lack of connectivity. Ultimately, the group decided to focus on finding a solution for the Abbott disk server, with the possibility of adding more storage or using a different disk server in the future."}
