{"input": "Why did the group disagree with the Project Manager when reflecting on the previous meetings and their project progress?", "answers": ["All the other three group members did not agree with the Project Manager that they thought they did not do enough as a team. Even though it might be because this was only a virtual project which did not require an actual building, as the Marketing said, it should be a much longer time of actual work rather than just imagining the remote control through three hours' meetings."], "length": 9197, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The group disagreed with the Project Manager when reflecting on the previous meetings and their project progress because they felt that the Project Manager was not allowing them to brainstorm and come up with new ideas, and instead was focusing too much on the technical aspects of the project. The group felt that this limited their creativity and ability to think outside the box, and that they were not being given the freedom to explore different concepts and ideas. Additionally, they felt that the Project Manager was not providing enough guidance and support, and that they were being left to figure things out on their own."}
{"input": "What's the decision of buttons size and scale design when discussing the design of the remote control?", "answers": ["It may require more than three millimetres with three buttons, and since there are not as many buttons, each button should be fully functional so that the basic requirements of the user can be met and the operation can be simple, or at least not too complicated, while they enjoy the function."], "length": 3242, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The decision on the buttons size and scale design is not explicitly stated in the meeting transcript. However, it is mentioned that the remote control should be small and not too big, with a size that can be held in one's hand, like a palm-sized device. It is also suggested that the buttons should be large enough to be easily pressed, but not so large that they are cumbersome. The Industrial Designer mentions that the buttons should be \"not too big like this\" and the User Interface agrees that the buttons should be \"just to hold it\". There is no clear consensus on the exact size or scale design of the buttons."}
{"input": "What did the Project Manager elaborate on the members when discussing the materials of the television remote?", "answers": ["The group talked about the material and they found it would be hard to balance the budget and the quality. In order to save the cost and ensure satisfying user experience, the Project Manager decided to choose high-quality recycled plastic as the material. But in terms of the battery, he would pay a lot to equip the remote with a cutting-edge lithium battery."], "length": 5341, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The Project Manager elaborated on the members when discussing the materials of the television remote by suggesting that they should use plastic, specifically high-quality recycled plastic, to keep costs down. This was based on the Industrial Designer's recommendation and the User Interface Developer's suggestion that plastic is a good option due to its potential to reduce interference with the remote's functionality. The Project Manager also mentioned that they could consider using modern types of polymers or plastics that have aesthetic value, but ultimately decided that plastic would be the most cost-effective option."}
{"input": "What did Bains say about the arts, culture, and tourism industry?", "answers": ["Bains claimed that the government was aware of these issues and had allocated $500 million to arts and culture organizations. Bains also explained that while pandemic control efforts were affecting these industries adversely, Canadians' health and safety remained the government's priority."], "length": 23788, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "Hon. Navdeep Bains stated that the government invested $500 million to respond to the specific financial needs of arts, heritage and sports organizations, to help them be more resilient through this difficult time. He also mentioned that the government is working to improve the risk management programs for agriculture, and that they are ready to do more to help the tourism sector."}
{"input": "Summarize the whole meeting.", "answers": ["The whole meeting was about a detailed prototype of the remote control. As before, this meeting also began with personal presentations. The Industrial Design focused on the components of the remote control, including the energy source, the buttons and the materials, while the User Interface suggested to use voice recognition technique and add secured or hidden programming onto the touch screen. Then the problem came that if they would like to make it so complex, they would go beyond the budget and have to raise the cost. Thus they decided to simplify some functions and buttons. Before the meeting ended, they also discussed the shape of the remote control."], "length": 7870, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting was about designing a new remote control with voice recognition and a unique, non-traditional design. The team discussed various aspects, including the casing material, buttons, and interface. They decided to go with a simple design with a rubber case, four basic buttons, and a drop-down menu on the side for more options. The team also considered using different case colors, such as natural wood or olive green, and possibly incorporating a natural, organic look. They ruled out the touch screen option due to cost concerns, instead opting for voice recognition as the main feature. The project manager assigned tasks to the team members, including Nathan to work on the basic look and feel, Ron to design the interface and layout, and the user interface team to create a prototype. The team will work together to create a functional prototype using prototype building materials and specific instructions will be sent to them by their coaches."}
{"input": "What did Morneau say about the debt?", "answers": ["Morneau explained that the government was committed to supporting Canadians. It came into the pandemic with a strong fiscal position, and while the pandemic will bring challenges, it will face those challenges while supporting small businesses and Canadians."], "length": 23784, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "Morneau stated that the government is in a fiscal position that enables it to take on debt at this time, which it thinks is appropriate to get the economy to a better position at the end of the crisis. He also mentioned that the government is investing in Canadians, which will allow them to have a stronger economy at the end. However, when asked directly about the size of the national debt, he did not provide a clear answer, and when asked if the government will hit $1 trillion of debt this year, he said that the government will continue to focus on supporting Canadians and making investments on their behalf, without providing a specific answer."}
{"input": "Summarize their discussions on pay dispute situations.", "answers": ["Dawn Bowden proposed the topic of pay dispute and asked what could be done as a Government to try to get parties back round the table and solve this dispute. Eluned Morgan thought this was about ColegauCymru's negotiation, and they were keeping a close eye on this situation. Eluned Morgan thought it would be fair to wait until they get further along down the line. Then Eluned Morgan had a detailed explanation about what they had done, including listening and speaking to ColegauCymru, and they were aware of what the unions were saying as well. Furthermore, Eluned Morgan said they would wish to see pay equality in relation to teaching, but details in relation to this should be waited until the outcome of the negotiations of ColegauCymru. They were aware of all those situations and they knew they were going to have to deal with it in the future."], "length": 13869, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The discussions on pay dispute situations centered around the pay dispute between ColegauCymru (the Welsh FE sector) and its staff, with the sector seeking a pay award of 3.5% or £10.1 million to meet the pay standards of schoolteachers. The Welsh Government, represented by the Cabinet Secretary for Education and the Minister for Children, Older People and Social Care, acknowledged the situation and expressed their willingness to support the sector in resolving the dispute, but emphasized that the decision on pay awards lies with ColegauCymru. The Minister noted that the sector's position is that an additional 3.5% or £10.1 million is needed to meet the pay standards of schoolteachers, and that the Welsh Government is keeping a close eye on the situation. The discussions also touched on the potential impact of the pay dispute on the sector's ability to recruit and retain staff, with the Minister expressing concern that the dispute could lead to a loss of talent and expertise in the sector."}
{"input": "What did the Project Manager think about their presentation contents when reflecting on their meetings and project progress?", "answers": ["The Project Manager planned to include their project process in the presentation. In addition, he thought it would be an interesting experiment to carry out an open mic presentation in which the team members could get out of the roles and share their satisfaction of the room and their creativity freely."], "length": 9196, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The Project Manager seemed to be somewhat underwhelmed and unimpressed with the presentation contents, mentioning that they didn't really understand the concept and felt like they were just copy-pasting information into their slides. They also felt that the project evaluation was not really about the project itself, but rather about cutting corners and meeting the budget. However, they did acknowledge that the team's creativity and ability to work together were strengths of the project."}
{"input": "What did the Industrial Designer and the Project Manager discuss about the LCD screen?", "answers": ["The User Interface Designer thought it might be in the middle of the product because the way users hold the product wouldn't influence the view to the screen, but the Project Manager and the Marketing thought the screen might be covered when held by hands, so the users couldn't figure out what happened on the screen. Then the Project Manager proposed that it was totally unusable, still needing marketing research."], "length": 10673, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The Industrial Designer and the Project Manager discussed the LCD screen, specifically whether to keep the advanced chip required for the LCD screen or to use a regular chip, which would make the device cheaper. They also considered the possibility of replacing the LCD screen with a simpler display, such as a school board, but ultimately decided to keep the LCD screen."}
{"input": "What did the group talk about as their reflection on the meetings and their progress?", "answers": ["The User Interface first pointed out that they did not use the whiteboard at all, neither did they use the pen as well. However, according to Marketing, it was quite understandable that due to the room constraints, such devices were not used. But the worse problem was that they did not receive as many notes as they wanted, the Marketing even received no reply after he wrote his coach."], "length": 9193, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The group reflected on their progress and discussed the challenges they faced during the meeting, including the fact that the project was not within budget and that they had to make some compromises, such as removing the solar panel feature. They also talked about the importance of teamwork and how they were able to work together effectively despite some initial difficulties. Additionally, they discussed the use of technology, such as the digital paper and the media player, and how it affected their workflow and productivity. They also shared their personal experiences and thoughts on the project, including the fact that they were all hooked on the internet and that it had changed the way they worked. Overall, the group was satisfied with their progress and felt that they had made good use of the time they had together."}
{"input": "Summarize the meeting", "answers": ["The participants went over the results of the most recent experiments, discussing future directions to take. Adding in more languages was still decreasing model performance. The best network consisted of the TIMIT and noise. The team thought that they should try to reduce their dependence on noise in the data. The Professor outlined how they could continue their experimentation."], "length": 14011, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting discussed the progress of a project related to speech recognition, specifically the use of neural networks and feature extraction techniques. The team presented results from various experiments, including those using different training sets, feature combinations, and noise robustness testing. They also discussed potential issues, such as the MSG problem, where the use of delta features did not improve performance, and the need for more robust training data. The team also touched on the integration of their work with the OGI system and the potential for using multi-band and belief-net structures. Additionally, they discussed the use of Linux machines for training and the need for more efficient computing resources. Overall, the meeting aimed to discuss the progress, challenges, and future directions of the project."}
{"input": "What were the three main causes for the financial challenges facing the universities?", "answers": ["Dr David Blaney introduced that the first was the impact of the demographic dip of 18-year-olds and as a result there was an increased pension cost generally. Second, current uncertainty also came as a result of the political environment like the Augar review in England and Brexit. This might deepen the funding gap. Third, due to the political decision to invest in students, universities were faced with challenges of providing more services under limited funding."], "length": 10205, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The three main causes for the financial challenges facing the universities in Wales are: (1) the demographic dip of 18-year-olds, which is deeper and longer in Wales than in the rest of the UK; (2) increased pension costs; and (3) increased costs generally, including the impact of the Augar review in England and Brexit."}
{"input": "What is Industrial Designer's presentation mainly about?", "answers": ["He talks about something on the components design after having put up the specification properties. As for materials, he used to suggest using hard plastic in order to make the control hard and solid, but at this conference, he thinks that their target audience, young people, love soft colors and materials, like rubber. And he also suggests a shape of a double curved case. As for the buttons, he suggests simple push buttons, without difficult scroll things that makes the control more complex and expensive. And he suggests not using a speaker or a sensor or speech controlled device."], "length": 11172, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "Industrial Designer's presentation is mainly about designing a remote control for a new electronic device, focusing on the user interface, materials, and features such as the L_C_D_ screen, buttons, and energy source."}
{"input": "Summarize the meeting", "answers": ["The meeting began with a discussion on the TORRENT project completion being pushed for two years. Grad F then introduced intermediate categorization, which was his topic for his qualification exams. The team then discussed mean subtraction from SRI. Using it had led to an improvement in Meeting Recorder digits though near mic performance worsened. The professor points to pre-echoes as the culprit. The team continued to study differences between SRI and Aurora. The team thought it would be interesting to do the Aurora tests with the SRI system instead of the HTK. The team was also exploring the Wiener filter and VTS. The professor did not seem too excited about the VTS."], "length": 11881, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting discussed various topics related to speech recognition and noise reduction. Professor B mentioned that they were two months away from completing a project, but it was actually two years away. The group discussed the Aurora system and its performance on the Meeting Recorder digits dataset, with improvements seen when using the SRI system instead of HTK. They also talked about the VAD problem and how it affects the system's performance, with some experiments showing that applying on-line normalization before VTS can improve results. Additionally, the group discussed the use of spectral subtraction and Wiener filtering to reduce noise, with some experiments showing promising results. They also touched on the idea of combining different methods to improve performance."}
{"input": "Summarize the decision discussion about key remote control concepts.", "answers": ["They decided to implement a LCD display with a scroll wheel. Instead of using hand dynamos, the group decided to use a wind dynamo which was more environmentally friendly. And they would keep the kinetic energy as an option and keep the spongy material preferences as well as voice recognition. At last, groupmates agreed to apply interchangeable cases with incorporated colours to make the remote more trendy. They would use a simple battery, the advanced chip, a curved side case and rubber buttons."], "length": 8979, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The decision discussion focused on key remote control concepts, including components, materials, user interface, and trends. The team decided to use an advanced chip with L_C_D_ displays, which would provide a sleek and modern look. They also considered using voice recognition, but ultimately decided to focus on a simple battery and push-buttons on the outside, with an L_C_D_ display and spinning wheel on the inside. The team also discussed the importance of ergonomics and usability, with a curved on one side case made of rubber and buttons also made of rubber. The final design would feature bright vegetable colors and a minimalist exterior that opens up to reveal a screen and spinning wheel."}
{"input": "What was agreed upon on sample transcripts?", "answers": ["To save time, speaker mn005 will only mark the sample of transcribed data for regions of overlapping speech, as opposed to marking all acoustic events. The digits extraction task will be delegated to whomever is working on acoustics for the Meeting Recorder project."], "length": 19654, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "There is no mention of sample transcripts being discussed or agreed upon in the provided meeting transcript."}
{"input": "What was the debate about government giving money to companies which did not put the amount into proper use?", "answers": ["The opposition party claimed that the government had been providing financial support to companies such as Air Canada, which did not pay a single cent in tax nor did it use the money to reimburse customers. The minister explained that the government did not bias against any company, , and it was thought that it was very important to protect employees in every sector of the economy and across Canada.The fight against tax evasion was a priority for the government. The minister promised that they would continue to target companies that use tax evasion schemes."], "length": 20281, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The debate was about the government giving money to companies, particularly those in the tourism and fishing industries, which were struggling due to the COVID-19 pandemic. However, some of these companies, such as those in the tourism industry, were seasonal and did not qualify for the emergency wage subsidy because their operations started in late May or early June. The Liberal Party of Canada, which did not need the money, had already received subsidies, leaving fishers and other seasonal workers to make do with less generous programs that did not meet their needs. The government's approach was criticized for prioritizing the needs of the Liberal Party over those of other Canadians who were struggling."}
{"input": "Why did Project Manager think of the advanced technology design when presenting the technical functions?", "answers": ["Industrial Designer suggested the group could keep the design as simple and clear as possible because this would help them to upgrade their technology at a future point of time. Project Manager asked about the cost at this point, however, Industrial Designer had no idea about what each component cost. So Project Manager thought it should be considered because the price would increase if they were using more advanced technology."], "length": 8491, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "Project Manager didn't explicitly think of advanced technology design when presenting the technical functions. Instead, the discussion about advanced technology design was initiated by the Industrial Designer, who mentioned that they had identified some basic components of the remote control and wanted to implement them in a way that was simple and easy to use. The Project Manager seemed to be open to the idea of incorporating advanced technology, such as voice recognition, but didn't explicitly suggest it as a design option."}
{"input": "What did Grad E contribute to the discussion on storage disks?", "answers": ["Grad E volunteered his 18 Gigabyte drive to the group. The drive had 12 gigabytes of memory and he was not using it for anything."], "length": 12805, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "Grad E mentioned that they have a lot of space on their computer, specifically an 18-gigabyte drive, and offered to use it to store data. They also mentioned that they had previously given 10 gigs of space to Thilo, and that they had used XG to store some data."}
{"input": "What did the group discuss about the functions of the remote control?", "answers": ["The User Interface proposed to build a stand-alone one, which can be different from any other devices. The Project Manager then added that it might be better with more useful functions like changing the faces. Marketing came up with the idea of making it be functional for other devices as well, just including everything in this remote control."], "length": 5985, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The group discussed the functions of the remote control, considering its potential to be a universal remote control that can control various devices such as TVs, microwaves, and front doors, and possibly even have features like a touch screen interface, a locator device, and a page button to help users find the remote. They also considered the trade-offs between size and functionality, and how to balance features with price, with the goal of creating a remote control that is both user-friendly and affordable, potentially priced around 25 Euros."}
{"input": "Summarize the discussion about product evaluation.", "answers": ["The marketing thought they needed to evaluate whether it made sense to do the project and whether the product could fulfil their requirement. So the group started to judge the design on a scale of one to seven, one being true and seven being false. The criteria were fanciness, technology, robustness, usefulness, size and weight, colour and shape, and adaptiveness. The product got an average score of two point one seven, which implied it was good."], "length": 8556, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The discussion about product evaluation focused on the strawberry remote control. The team evaluated its features, including its design, functionality, and usability. They used a scale from 1 to 7 to rate its performance, with 1 being \"not at all\" and 7 being \"very good\". The team members discussed the product's features, such as its ability to control the L_C_D_ display, its use of speech recognition, and its location-finding capabilities. They also evaluated its usefulness, with some members suggesting that it could be improved by adding features such as a hand dynamo or a battery. The team ultimately decided to give the product a score of 2.1 out of 7, indicating that it was a good but not perfect product."}
{"input": "What are the group's decisions on LSD screen, color and materials?", "answers": ["As for the LCD screen, the Project Manager considers colored ones are a bit too expensive, so they can just do normal ones, and the shape of the control can be in a bridge shape. As for the materials, Industrial Designers think that a solid and strong appearance is necessary, and Marketing agrees that plastics don't create a strong touching feeling, and as a combination, they decide to have hard plastic for the front and then titanium for the back. As for colors, the group decides to use basic colors with some special patterns."], "length": 11176, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The group decides to use an L_C_D_ screen, and the color is to be bright and fruity, with a focus on primary colors. The materials for the remote control are to be titanium for the back and plastic for the front. The group also decides that the front should be designed to be easy to use and have a strong look, with a focus on making it feel strong and luxurious."}
