{"input": "Why did the Project Manager put forward to cut down the functions when discussing the design of the functions and buttons of the remote control?", "answers": ["Due to the limited budget as well as to achieve a satisfying user experience, the Project Manager proposed only to keep the most essential functions in case they would be beyond the capacity of the microchip."], "length": 5349, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The Project Manager suggested cutting down the functions of the remote control because the marketing team had found that most users only use a few basic functions such as switching on the television, changing the channel, and adjusting the volume, and that the other functions are not used frequently or are not known to the users. This was based on the results of a usability test and a questionnaire that the marketing team had conducted, which showed that users are not interested in complicated remotes with many buttons."}
{"input": "How did PhD B approach the back-end of the Aurora recognizer?", "answers": ["PhD B focused on Italian and experimented with the number of states for different words. PhD B thought training for each case may improve performance by accounting for the difference in variance."], "length": 8191, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "PhD B approached the back-end of the Aurora recognizer by modifying the HTK system and running it again with optimized parameters, specifically by reducing the number of states in some of the shorter models to see how it affected the performance. They also experimented with different models, including those with nine states, which they found to be better than the original eighteen states used in the well-matched case. Additionally, they planned to play with the spectral subtraction and retry the MSG, and to create new baseline for next week with modified models."}
{"input": "What was the discussion about imports and supply chains?", "answers": ["The opposition party claimed that the supply chain in Canada amidst the pandemic was not stable enough and the government was not doing anything. The minister explained that they would continue to work with countries around the globe to ensure that Canada's supply chains and those global supply chains, particularly for essential goods, for agricultural products, for medical supplies, would continue to remain open."], "length": 20271, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The discussion about imports and supply chains was a significant topic in the meeting. The Canadian government was facing challenges in securing personal protective equipment (PPE) and other essential supplies due to the COVID-19 pandemic, and the global competition for these supplies was making it difficult to meet the demand. The Minister of Public Service and Procurement, Anita Anand, explained that the government was diversifying supply chains internationally and building up and retooling domestic industry to ensure a steady supply of PPE and other essential goods. The government was also exploring ways to assist broader organizations across the country with PPE needs. The Minister also acknowledged that some government orders for N95 masks had been dropping, but attributed this to the global competition for these supplies."}
{"input": "Summarize the whole meeting.", "answers": ["The team introduced their findings in turns and gradually came to some agreements. First, Industrial Designer introduced the structure of the device and suggested one battery and small size. Meanwhile, Project Manager questioned the cover design since it would not be cheap. Then, User Interface left a question whether the technical function should be basic or multi-functional. After that, Marketing concluded that less important functions should be discarded and the device should be user friendly. Lastly, Project Manager suggested discarding the teletext and asked for ideas about button design."], "length": 4751, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting was a discussion on designing a remote control for televisions. The Industrial Designer presented his findings on the technical function design of a remote control, highlighting the difficulties in explaining the remote control's working mechanism. The Marketing expert presented the findings of a usability lab-test with 100 persons, showing that users disliked the look and feel of current remote controls and found them hard to use. The User Interface expert discussed the technical requirements for the remote control, including power, channel, and volume buttons, as well as a menu button. The group decided to aim for a younger market, with a focus on ease of use and a nice-looking remote control. They also discussed the costs and decided to limit the number of buttons to make the remote control more affordable. The meeting concluded with the Industrial Designer and Marketing expert agreeing to move forward with the conceptual design phase, while the User Interface expert was tasked with creating the individual action items."}
{"input": "What did the team think about their progress?", "answers": ["The professor asked if the team was happy with their progress. The team thought that they were okay. The professor was insistent that everyone be happy since they were pretty much done."], "length": 14016, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The team seemed to be generally satisfied with their progress, with some members expressing concerns about the complexity of the task and the need to focus on specific areas, such as training targets and noise dependency. However, they also acknowledged that they had made some progress and were able to identify some potential issues, such as the MSG problem and the need for better normalization. The team also discussed the potential benefits of using different temporal properties and the importance of selecting the most promising approaches to pursue further. Overall, the team seemed to be making progress, but also recognizing the need for further work and refinement."}
{"input": "What did the team discuss during the product evaluation?", "answers": ["The team agreed that only the scroll button and the LCD were new items for a remote control. The color of the device was doubted but Marketing argued that since the product aimed at the young market, the case looked good in pure yellow. Besides, the rubber material felt soft, making the device look and feel nice. However, the team thought that there were too many buttons, which did not align with the original idea."], "length": 4807, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The team discussed the evaluation of a product, specifically a remote control, and rated it based on various criteria such as design, functionality, and innovation. They evaluated the product's features, including the L_C_D_ display, scroll-wheel, and push-button, and discussed the pros and cons of different design options, such as keeping the joystick or replacing it with buttons. The team also evaluated the product's usability, user experience, and overall value for money, with some members giving it a high rating of 4 or 5 out of 7, while others gave it a lower rating of 1 or 2."}
{"input": "What did the team say about the new product requirements?", "answers": ["Project Manager decided that the remote control should only be used on television and targeted at the biggest size of group. Corporate colour and slogan must be used on the cover. They agreed that a power button, channel switches from zero to nine, volume control, mute should be contained and a small-size menu included."], "length": 4757, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The team discussed the new product requirements, which included the removal of teletext since internet is now available, and the focus on only television sets for the remote control, targeting a younger age group between 16 and 45. They also decided to use the L_C_D_ screen and not too many buttons, with a focus on ease of use, and considered adding a mute function in the menu. Additionally, they decided to use the corporate color and slogan in the design."}
{"input": "What was the discussion about the seniors care crisis?", "answers": ["The opposition party claimed that the seniors care crisis was a national problem, and the federal government was not taking immediate response. The opposition party pointed out that these failures were the product of systemic neglect.The minister replied that they were fully aware that in long-term care facilities both seniors and persons living with a disability face unique challenges. And considering the severity of this report, the federal government promptly shared it with the Province of Ontario, and the Province of Ontario has initiated an investigation based on the report's findings."], "length": 20271, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The discussion about the seniors care crisis centered around the horrific conditions in long-term care homes in Ontario and other provinces, as revealed in a report by the Canadian Armed Forces. The report detailed instances of neglect, abuse, and danger faced by seniors in care, including missed medications, expired medications, unsterile devices, and violations of basic contagion rules. The government, led by the Minister of Health, acknowledged the severity of the situation and committed to working with provinces and territories to improve care and prevent further tragic occurrences. The Minister also stated that the government would take steps to ensure that every person has the right to age with dignity and safety, but did not provide specific details on how this would be achieved."}
{"input": "What did the group conclude on LCD screens and the speech recognition suggested by Marketing?", "answers": ["Marketing mentioned that the research found it would be costly for the speech design and suggested considering LCD screens. Industrial Design suggested that they would consider both and see what they could find. The group all agreed on it.pressing the button."], "length": 11310, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The group concluded that they should include an LCD screen on the remote control, with the screen being placed at the top, and that they should consider using an LCD screen rather than speech recognition, as the latter was deemed too costly and not yet a standard development."}
{"input": "Summarize the discussion about appearance design.", "answers": ["To follow the trend of fruit and vegetable, there were two options: something in titanium and smelling like fruit, or something spongy and fruity-like. The industrial designer would explore these two choices and he also suggested having two different assemblies, but the project manager said they couldn't have both. The project manager also mentioned another solution - painting the controller to pretend that it was titanium. The group didn't make a final decision."], "length": 6954, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The discussion about appearance design focused on creating a remote control that is both functional and visually appealing. The team considered various options, including a titanium design that could be shaped like a fruit, such as a banana, and a spongy design that could be made to resemble a fruit. They also explored the idea of using a combination of materials, such as titanium panels on a rubber body. The team ultimately decided to keep the L_C_D_ display, but to make it more user-friendly by providing information on the current action. The design should be simple, with a limited number of buttons, and should not be too futuristic or complicated. The team also considered the trend of using natural materials and shapes, and the idea of making the remote control change color depending on the environment."}
{"input": "What did the team say about the project and overall process?", "answers": ["The team thought they had a really great team work experience. Everyone had put efforts into the process and gave opinions to design a good remote control. Also, the project manager showed good leadership to control the overall process."], "length": 4809, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The team generally thought the project was good, with the Industrial Designer and User Interface praising the creativity and the Project Manager noting that it was good for the speed. The Marketing team mentioned that the project was well-organized and that they were able to come up with new ideas, but also noted that the laptops and devices used during the project made it difficult to focus on the presentation. The User Interface also mentioned that the team's participation was good, with everyone having a chance to share their opinions. Overall, the team seemed to be satisfied with the project and the process, with the Industrial Designer stating that the process was \"went good\" and the Marketing team agreeing that they were able to evaluate the product effectively."}
{"input": "Summarize the whole meeting.", "answers": ["The main points of the discussion are the design goal and price of a new television remote control project. The group first put forward the design goal of remote control. Then they got used to the whiteboard and wrote down everyone's favourite animal and their characteristics. Project manager and Marketing wanted to sell this remote control for twenty five Euro and expected profit will be around two million Euro. Then, the group thought about colour and function features of the new remote controls. In addition, they also believed that the remote control should be safe enough for children to use, and the appearance should be acceptable to them."], "length": 3229, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting was a kick-off meeting for the design of a new remote control. The project aims to create an original, trendy, and user-friendly remote control that can be controlled by a brain or a screen, with features such as a go back button, history, and recording capabilities. The team discussed various ideas, including a universal remote control that can be used for multiple devices, and considered factors such as size, color, and functionality. They also talked about the importance of making the remote control robust and safe for children, and considered features such as a child lock and a screen that can display different options. The project manager assigned tasks to the team members, including the user interface designer, marketing expert, and industrial designer, and set a deadline of thirty minutes for them to work on the ideas and decide on the most important features."}
{"input": "What did the team discuss about the product cost?", "answers": ["In terms of the material used on the device, the team decided to use only one material, either rubber or plastic instead of both or titanium. Moreover, the team agreed to discard the joystick but keep the LCD and advance chips,to make it still favored by the young market. Lastly, a normal color would be incorporated instead of a special color to decrease the cost by at least half Euro."], "length": 4807, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The team discussed the product cost, specifically the price of the product, and decided that it was too expensive at 15 Euros. They then brainstormed ways to reduce the cost, such as changing the joystick to a button layout, which would save 0.5 Euros, making the final cost 12.5 Euros."}
{"input": "Please describe the semantic specification", "answers": ["The semantic specification, on the other hand, is split into three levels: \"scenario\" is a list of schemas and bindings between them, which describes the current event in terms of Source-Path-Goal, Container, etc.; \"referent\" is about the entities in the discourse and includes grammatical information and pointers to the ontology; \"discourse segment\" comprises utterance-specific things."], "length": 24579, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The semantic specification is a tool kit for building the semantic part of constructions, which includes a set of slots and bindings that capture the meaning of a sentence or phrase. It consists of a scenario, which is a mental space that represents the context in which the sentence is being used, and a set of discourse segments, which are the individual parts of the sentence that contribute to its meaning. The semantic specification also includes a set of constraints, such as polarity and focus, that help to determine the meaning of the sentence. Additionally, it includes a set of constructions, such as cause and effect, that capture the relationships between different parts of the sentence. The semantic specification is intended to be a flexible and scalable framework for representing the meaning of sentences, and it can be used to generate a wide range of possible interpretations."}
