{"input": "Summarize the whole meeting.", "answers": ["The meeting was mainly about the exchange of the preliminary ideas about a new TV remote control project. They first got used to the writeboard and drew some animals with it.Project manager wanted to sell this remote control for twenty five Euro and expected profit will be around fifty million Euro. Afterwards the team raised different opinions about features of the new remote controls and related questions about market potential. Among all the features, having a good look and size were unanimously considered to be the most essential."], "length": 6381, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The meeting was a kick-off meeting for a new project to design a new television remote control. The team discussed the project's goals, target audience, and design requirements, including making it original, trendy, and modern. They also talked about the remote's functionality, including infrared technology for universal compatibility, and the importance of a user-friendly interface with clear buttons and a simple design. The team brainstormed ideas for the remote's design, including using a front with a specific color scheme, and discussed the need for a universal design that would appeal to a wide audience. They also discussed the project's technical requirements, including the use of a universal remote protocol, and the need for a user interface that is easy to use and understand. The meeting concluded with a plan to continue discussing the project's details in the next meeting, which would be held in 30 minutes."}
{"input": "What did Kirsty Williams say about the trend of teacher recruiting, the reasons for it, and the steps they had taken?", "answers": ["Even though there was no specific figure that could be provided, they had only been recruiting about 65 percent of targets.Therefore, there was a lot of work they have to do about this. First, they were making sure that their ITE provision was world class, and recently they were through an accreditation process for a new ITE provision that would start in the next academic year. Second, they had looked at financial incentives.Third, they were embarking on their first national ITE recruitment marketing exercise. Kirsty Williams mentioned that this was not a unique issue in Wales, but a common issue across the globe. Money was not the only reason that prevented people from getting onto these courses. What's more, from next year, they would be going to have their unique part-time PGCE route into qualification, which allowed people to bring their outside world experience into teaching, and this could increase the diversity in their teaching workforce."], "length": 13883, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "Kirsty Williams stated that the trend of teacher recruiting, specifically for secondary school teachers, was that only about 65% of the priority places were being filled, and that this was a problem that needed to be addressed. She attributed the issue to a lack of money alone, as the problem was also seen in England, and that research showed that it was not just about financial incentives. She mentioned that the Welsh Government had taken steps to address the issue, including making sure that their ITE provision was \"world class\", providing financial incentives, and embarking on a national ITE recruitment marketing exercise. Additionally, she mentioned that they had set up an advisory board on the recruitment and retention of teaching staff to identify the issues and find solutions."}
{"input": "What did the team discuss about the use of advanced chips and LCD display?", "answers": ["Industrial Designer introduced both simple chips and advanced chips could be used for the mouse. But it would require the use of LCD display, which would highly increase the cost. Project Manager agreed that the LCD was easy when using the scroll buttons and could see the number. But Project Manager argued that young people were less likely to have their own room to afford a LCD TV and decided not to choose the advanced ones."], "length": 6036, "dataset": "qmsum", "pred": "The team discussed the use of advanced chips and LCD display, with the Industrial Designer mentioning that using an LCD display would increase the costs, and the Project Manager noting that the television must be able to handle the display, but it's not clear if it's possible. The Industrial Designer suggested using a regular chip instead of an advanced chip to reduce costs, and the Project Manager agreed that the cost of the LCD display would depend on the specific design."}
